{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015xrFG9G2Gshpb61RMjh9KF","type":"tool_result","content":"340\t    # SN-026: an adjudicator rules on a CLAIM — was this delivered, did this\n341\t    # amendment move meaning, is this queued row a duplicate — and every one of\n342\t    # those is a judgement whose cost of being wrong is a wrong approval.\n343\t    # Strong by default, like the other two judging phases. The per-row\n344\t    # `BuildTier` still pins it down where a disposition estimated cheaper\n345\t    # (`intake.tier_signal`), because that estimate is measured; this is the\n346\t    # floor for a row that names nothing.\n347\t    \"ADJUDICATE\": \"strong\",\n348\t}\n349\t\n350\t# A model whose session fails to start / stalls goes on cooldown this long (its\n351\t# limit is probably exhausted) — the generalized rate-limit backoff, per-model.\n352\t# AGENT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS overrides; a bad value falls back to this default.\n353\tDEFAULT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS = 900\n354\t\n355\t# Phases that are NOT build work, so a commit in them never triggers a review\n356\t# round through the BUILD arm (a reviewer's own commit, a planner, an\n357\t# integrator, a critic writing its verdict). DESIGN-CHECK stays in the set\n358\t# because it is not a build for TIER/routing purposes, but a committing one\n359\t# arms the round through its own arm in `build_bookkeeping` — it did the\n360\t# rework, and a BUILD session that exists only to re-arm the round is waste.\n361\tNON_BUILD_PHASES = frozenset(kverdict.REVIEW_PHASES) | {\n362\t    \"PLAN\",\n363\t    \"INTEGRATE\",\n364\t    \"DESIGN-CHECK\",\n365\t    \"CRITIQUE\",\n366\t    # SN-026: an adjudication commit changes Status cells and the work\n367\t    # registry, which is what its lane runs no product bar for\n368\t    # (`integrate.refresh`'s no-bar arm). A review round over it would be a\n369\t    # fresh-context reviewer asked to judge a judgement, with no product diff\n370\t    # to judge — the corroboration loop the review rounds exist to avoid.\n371\t    \"ADJUDICATE\",\n372\t}\n373\t\n374\t\n375\t# (read_ask retired with the serial driver, WI-210: the engine composes\n376\t# its NEEDS-HUMAN banners from the ask it just generated — the `ask:` line in\n377\t# docs/run-state remains the WI-127 contract for humans and launchers.)\n378\t\n379\t\n380\t# (--track and its docs/tracks/<name>/ lane plumbing retired outright, WI-210:\n381\t# the explicit --wi worker assignment is the only lane\n382\t# concept; docs/ is the one coordination surface and the integrator owns it.)\n383\t\n384\t\n385\tdef assignment_block(root, wi_rows, wi, base, assigned):\n386\t    \"\"\"The WI-580 batch block: EVERY row this lane was claimed with, each with\n387\t    its evidence state, or `\"\"` for the ordinary one-row lane.\n388\t\n389\t    The dispatcher admits a spine batch as ONE lane (`--wi 'A;B'`, §A4) and\n390\t    `current_assignment_wi` walks it a row per session — but the brief rendered\n391\t    the walked row alone, under an opening sentence that called it the whole\n392\t    scope. Measured 2026-09-02 on `wi-569-…`: the human saw `wi=WI-569;WI-575`\n393\t    in the launch banner and the session that took WI-569 never learned WI-575\n394\t    was on its lane.\n395\t\n396\t    THE ONE-ROW LANE RENDERS NOTHING, which is what keeps this safe to add: the\n397\t    `- WI:`/`- SR-Refs:`/`- Branch:` lines already carry every fact this block\n398\t    would repeat, so only a batch can observe the difference.\n399\t\n400\t    The state vocabulary is the walk's own, not a fourth opinion about\n401\t    doneness: `this session's focus` is whatever `current_assignment_wi`\n402\t    returned, and the rest split on the SAME committed-trailer evidence that\n403\t    walk reads (`train_evidence`). A row that is `built` here is one the walk\n404\t    has already stepped past.\n405\t\n406\t    Implements: SR-026, LLR-061\n407\t    \"\"\"\n408\t    if len(assigned) < 2:\n409\t        return \"\"\n410\t    built, _blocked = train_evidence(root, base)\n411\t    return (\n412\t        \"- The WHOLE assignment ({} rows claimed on this lane, one row per \"\n413\t        \"session — a sibling row is this lane's later work, not another \"\n414\t        \"lane's):\\n\".format(len(assigned))\n415\t        + \"\".join(\n416\t            \"  - {} [{}] {} — SpecRef: {}\\n\".format(\n417\t                tok,\n418\t                \"this session's focus\"\n419\t                if tok == wi\n420\t                else (\"built\" if tok in built else \"not started\"),\n421\t                _row_title(wi_rows, tok),\n422\t                (wi_rows.get(tok, {}).get(\"SpecRef\") or \"—\").strip() or \"—\",\n423\t            )\n424\t            for tok in assigned\n425\t        )\n426\t    )\n427\t\n428\t\n429\tdef _row_title(wi_rows, tok):\n430\t    \"\"\"A WI's Title for a prompt block, with the placeholder both blocks show\n431\t    for a row the registry does not carry — an empty cell there would read as a\n432\t    row with no scope rather than as a row the reader cannot look up.\"\"\"\n433\t    return (\n434\t        wi_rows.get(tok, {}).get(\"Title\") or \"(row missing from the registry)\"\n435\t    ).strip()\n436\t\n437\t\n438\tdef worker_prompt(root, wi_rows, wi, train, base, rework_text=\"\", assigned=None):\n439\t    \"\"\"The per-session worker prompt (LLR-061): the WI row + SpecRef +\n440\t    predecessor context + the current branch diff + any rework finding, slotted\n441\t    into WORKER_PROMPT (`train` is the session tag = the claim branch name).\n442\t    Reads NOTHING from docs/status.md or docs/next-wi — the explicit\n443\t    assignment is the whole scope.\n444\t\n445\t    `assigned` is the lane's WHOLE claim (WI-580); `wi` is the row this session\n446\t    walked to. Defaulting it to `[wi]` keeps every in-process caller that only\n447\t    knows one row rendering exactly what it rendered before.\n448\t\n449\t    Implements: SR-026, LLR-061\n450\t    \"\"\"\n451\t    row = wi_rows.get(wi, {})\n452\t\n453\t    preds = []\n454\t    for tok in re.split(r\"[;,\\s]+\", (row.get(\"Predecessors\") or \"\").strip()):\n455\t        tok = tok.lstrip(\"~\")\n456\t        if tok and WI_TOKEN_RE.match(tok):\n457\t            p = wi_rows.get(tok)\n458\t            if p is not None:\n459\t                deliverable = (p.get(\"Deliverable\") or \"\").strip()\n460\t                if len(deliverable) > 200:\n461\t                    deliverable = deliverable[:200] + \"…\"\n462\t                preds.append(\n463\t                    \"  - {} [{}] {}{}\".format(\n464\t                        tok,\n465\t                        (p.get(\"Status\") or \"?\").strip(),\n466\t                        (p.get(\"Title\") or \"\").strip(),\n467\t                        \" — \" + deliverable if deliverable else \"\",\n468\t                    )\n469\t                )"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"abce9961-c62e-4c5b-befe-0c3785810420","uuid":"96f8a495-b289-4212-91fb-6eec71ec1a04","timestamp":"2026-09-05T04:17:54.893Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-580-the-worker-and-reviewer-briefs/project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py","content":"    # SN-026: an adjudicator rules on a CLAIM — was this delivered, did this\n    # amendment move meaning, is this queued row a duplicate — and every one of\n    # those is a judgement whose cost of being wrong is a wrong approval.\n    # Strong by default, like the other two judging phases. The per-row\n    # `BuildTier` still pins it down where a disposition estimated cheaper\n    # (`intake.tier_signal`), because that estimate is measured; this is the\n    # floor for a row that names nothing.\n    \"ADJUDICATE\": \"strong\",\n}\n\n# A model whose session fails to start / stalls goes on cooldown this long (its\n# limit is probably exhausted) — the generalized rate-limit backoff, per-model.\n# AGENT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS overrides; a bad value falls back to this default.\nDEFAULT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS = 900\n\n# Phases that are NOT build work, so a commit in them never triggers a review\n# round through the BUILD arm (a reviewer's own commit, a planner, an\n# integrator, a critic writing its verdict). DESIGN-CHECK stays in the set\n# because it is not a build for TIER/routing purposes, but a committing one\n# arms the round through its own arm in `build_bookkeeping` — it did the\n# rework, and a BUILD session that exists only to re-arm the round is waste.\nNON_BUILD_PHASES = frozenset(kverdict.REVIEW_PHASES) | {\n    \"PLAN\",\n    \"INTEGRATE\",\n    \"DESIGN-CHECK\",\n    \"CRITIQUE\",\n    # SN-026: an adjudication commit changes Status cells and the work\n    # registry, which is what its lane runs no product bar for\n    # (`integrate.refresh`'s no-bar arm). A review round over it would be a\n    # fresh-context reviewer asked to judge a judgement, with no product diff\n    # to judge — the corroboration loop the review rounds exist to avoid.\n    \"ADJUDICATE\",\n}\n\n\n# (read_ask retired with the serial driver, WI-210: the engine composes\n# its NEEDS-HUMAN banners from the ask it just generated — the `ask:` line in\n# docs/run-state remains the WI-127 contract for humans and launchers.)\n\n\n# (--track and its docs/tracks/<name>/ lane plumbing retired outright, WI-210:\n# the explicit --wi worker assignment is the only lane\n# concept; docs/ is the one coordination surface and the integrator owns it.)\n\n\ndef assignment_block(root, wi_rows, wi, base, assigned):\n    \"\"\"The WI-580 batch block: EVERY row this lane was claimed with, each with\n    its evidence state, or `\"\"` for the ordinary one-row lane.\n\n    The dispatcher admits a spine batch as ONE lane (`--wi 'A;B'`, §A4) and\n    `current_assignment_wi` walks it a row per session — but the brief rendered\n    the walked row alone, under an opening sentence that called it the whole\n    scope. Measured 2026-09-02 on `wi-569-…`: the human saw `wi=WI-569;WI-575`\n    in the launch banner and the session that took WI-569 never learned WI-575\n    was on its lane.\n\n    THE ONE-ROW LANE RENDERS NOTHING, which is what keeps this safe to add: the\n    `- WI:`/`- SR-Refs:`/`- Branch:` lines already carry every fact this block\n    would repeat, so only a batch can observe the difference.\n\n    The state vocabulary is the walk's own, not a fourth opinion about\n    doneness: `this session's focus` is whatever `current_assignment_wi`\n    returned, and the rest split on the SAME committed-trailer evidence that\n    walk reads (`train_evidence`). A row that is `built` here is one the walk\n    has already stepped past.\n\n    Implements: SR-026, LLR-061\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(assigned) < 2:\n        return \"\"\n    built, _blocked = train_evidence(root, base)\n    return (\n        \"- The WHOLE assignment ({} rows claimed on this lane, one row per \"\n        \"session — a sibling row is this lane's later work, not another \"\n        \"lane's):\\n\".format(len(assigned))\n        + \"\".join(\n            \"  - {} [{}] {} — SpecRef: {}\\n\".format(\n                tok,\n                \"this session's focus\"\n                if tok == wi\n                else (\"built\" if tok in built else \"not started\"),\n                _row_title(wi_rows, tok),\n                (wi_rows.get(tok, {}).get(\"SpecRef\") or \"—\").strip() or \"—\",\n            )\n            for tok in assigned\n        )\n    )\n\n\ndef _row_title(wi_rows, tok):\n    \"\"\"A WI's Title for a prompt block, with the placeholder both blocks show\n    for a row the registry does not carry — an empty cell there would read as a\n    row with no scope rather than as a row the reader cannot look up.\"\"\"\n    return (\n        wi_rows.get(tok, {}).get(\"Title\") or \"(row missing from the registry)\"\n    ).strip()\n\n\ndef worker_prompt(root, wi_rows, wi, train, base, rework_text=\"\", assigned=None):\n    \"\"\"The per-session worker prompt (LLR-061): the WI row + SpecRef +\n    predecessor context + the current branch diff + any rework finding, slotted\n    into WORKER_PROMPT (`train` is the session tag = the claim branch name).\n    Reads NOTHING from docs/status.md or docs/next-wi — the explicit\n    assignment is the whole scope.\n\n    `assigned` is the lane's WHOLE claim (WI-580); `wi` is the row this session\n    walked to. Defaulting it to `[wi]` keeps every in-process caller that only\n    knows one row rendering exactly what it rendered before.\n\n    Implements: SR-026, LLR-061\n    \"\"\"\n    row = wi_rows.get(wi, {})\n\n    preds = []\n    for tok in re.split(r\"[;,\\s]+\", (row.get(\"Predecessors\") or \"\").strip()):\n        tok = tok.lstrip(\"~\")\n        if tok and WI_TOKEN_RE.match(tok):\n            p = wi_rows.get(tok)\n            if p is not None:\n                deliverable = (p.get(\"Deliverable\") or \"\").strip()\n                if len(deliverable) > 200:\n                    deliverable = deliverable[:200] + \"…\"\n                preds.append(\n                    \"  - {} [{}] {}{}\".format(\n                        tok,\n                        (p.get(\"Status\") or \"?\").strip(),\n                        (p.get(\"Title\") or \"\").strip(),\n                        \" — \" + deliverable if deliverable else \"\",\n                    )\n                )","numLines":130,"startLine":340,"totalLines":4537}}}
